---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Google Ads for Medical Practices | Medical Rank" description="Google Ads management for US medical practices. Discuss campaigns, landing pages, spend and enquiry reporting with Medical Rank.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="pagehead">
      <h1>Google Ads for medical practices.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Reach people searching for the care your practice offers, with campaigns built around your services and locations.</p>
      <p>Medical Rank manages search campaigns for US medical practices. We work on campaign structure, search terms, ad copy and the pages patients reach after clicking, with reporting that explains what your account is counting.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk about your practice</a>
        <a class="btn quiet" href="#scope">Explore the work</a>
      </div>
    </header>
  </div>

  <section class="section" id="scope">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>A clear scope for your search campaigns.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Whether you already run ads or are considering a first campaign, we discuss what the practice needs before deciding on the work.</p>
      <div class="cols">
        <dl class="deflist">
          <div><dt>Campaign setup and management</dt><dd>Organize campaigns around the services and locations you want to advertise, then review the account and make changes within the agreed scope.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Search terms and ad copy</dt><dd>Review the searches associated with your ads and the messages people see, with attention to relevance to the care your practice provides.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <dl class="deflist">
          <div><dt>Landing pages</dt><dd>Review what patients see after a click and how they can contact the practice. Page recommendations or improvements are agreed as part of the scope.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Spend and enquiry reporting</dt><dd>Explain the actions your account counts, review spend against those measures and distinguish clicks, calls and requests from booked appointments.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div>
        <h2 class="label">Where we begin</h2>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li><div><strong>Understand the practice</strong>Discuss your services, locations, appointment priorities and what you want advertising to help with.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Review the account and website</strong>Look at any existing campaigns, their settings and the pages people reach from the ads.</div></li>
          <li><div><strong>Agree on the work and measures</strong>Outline campaign priorities, page work and how progress will be reviewed before the engagement begins.</div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="label">Useful for the first conversation</h2>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>Your practice website and the services you want to advertise.</li>
          <li>Any current Google Ads reports and management scope.</li>
          <li>The budget you are considering, including advertising spend.</li>
          <li>What you know about appointment requests and where their source is unclear.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="note">You do not need to diagnose the account before contacting us. Tell us what you have and what you want to improve.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Before we work together.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Can you review campaigns an agency already manages?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Tell us how the account is managed today, what work is already covered and what you want a closer look at. We can discuss the appropriate next step before agreeing on a new scope.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How will I know whether the ads produce appointments?</summary>
          <p>We start by clarifying what the account counts. A call or form submission is different from a booking. If the available records do not connect ad activity to appointments, we explain the gap and what would be needed to investigate it.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How are management fees and advertising spend handled?</summary>
          <p>They are different costs. We outline the scope and agency fee, and discuss the advertising budget separately, before you decide whether to proceed.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need local SEO too?</summary>
          <p>That depends on your current presence and priorities. We also offer <a href="/services/local-seo/">local SEO</a>, and the first conversation can help decide where to start.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you guarantee a number of new patients?</summary>
          <p>No. We agree on the work and how it will be assessed. The reports show specific recorded actions; we explain their limits when reviewing progress.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <p class="note">For a closer look at what the reports count, read <a href="/guides/is-google-ads-bringing-in-booked-appointments/">Is Google Ads bringing in booked appointments?</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Let's talk about your campaigns.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Tell us what you advertise, what you want to improve and what your current reports show. Our first conversation is about where to start and whether we can help. No obligation.</p>
      <a class="btn quiet" href="/contact/">Talk about your practice</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
